		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T10:36:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Remove Cocoon file event stubs, normalize Mountain IPC\n\nAdvance Cocoon and Mountain submodules with a coordinated fix and refactor.\n\n**Cocoon file event fix:**\nSix stub file lifecycle event handlers (`onWillCreateFiles`, `onWillDeleteFiles`, `onWillRenameFiles`, `onDidCreateFiles`, `onDidDeleteFiles`, `onDidRenameFiles`) on the Workspace namespace were returning no-op disposables, overriding the real `EventSubscriber` implementations already provided by the `BuildDocumentEventMembers` spread. Extensions subscribing to these events — including GitLens — were silently receiving dead handlers that emitted nothing. Remove the stubs so live events flow through. Mountain now fires `willCreate`/`willDelete`/`willRename` notifications via Vine before VFS mutation.\n\n**Mountain IPC handler normalization (refactor):**\nRename the three Cocoon IPC entry points from descriptive names (`CocoonExtensionHostMessage`, `CocoonNotify`, `CocoonRequest`) to the uniform `Fn` ident, with matching `as` aliases in mod.rs re-exports so downstream callers are unaffected.\n\nAdd four new ExtensionHost IPC handlers also exporting as `Fn`:\n- DebugServiceClose: emits `sky://exthost/debug-close` via Tauri Emitter\n- DebugServiceReload: emits `SkyEvent::ExtHostDebugReload` for cache purging\n- StarterCreate: returns stub extension-host ID (`\"1\"`)\n- StarterStart: returns real Cocoon PID for debugger attachment\n\nAll handler modules now follow a single convention, eliminating naming guesswork when adding new IPC routes.",
			"SHA": "346e1280854bf61586f46bbbb49171c5b34788fe"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T10:31:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Fix Cocoon bootstrap stage ordering and cache Mountain extension metadata\n\nAdvance Cocoon and Mountain submodules with a coordinated fix and performance update across the extension host bootstrap and metadata pipeline.\n\n**Cocoon bootstrap stage reordering (fix):**\nThe Stage 3 MountainConnection gRPC probe previously ran ahead of Stage 5 RPCServer in the bootstrap pipeline, causing Mountain's 20-second gRPC retry budget to exhaust on every startup since port 50052 was never bound within the connect window. Swap the execution order in `makeBootstrap` so RPCServer binds first, then MountainConnection connects to a live listener. Reduce retry caps proportionally: TCP probe from 10 to 3 attempts, gRPC connect from 15 to 5 attempts.\n\n**Mountain extension cache (perf):**\nBuilding the serialized `ILocalExtension[]` array on every `extensions:getInstalled` IPC call re-serialized ~1.8 MB of extension metadata, causing multi-hundred-millisecond UI stalls on startup. Add a `OnceLock`-backed static cache keyed by TypeFilter variant (None, System, User). First call per type populates the cache; subsequent calls return a cloned `Value` in <1 ms. Empty responses are not cached to avoid poisoning on first-call timeout.\n\n**Mountain reliability fixes:**\n- `FileCloneNative` now creates the target parent directory via `tokio::fs::create_dir_all` before `fs::copy`, resolving ENOENT failures for VS Code's per-file history directories.\n- CocoonManagement IO forwarders switch from `tokio::spawn` to `tauri::async_runtime::spawn` so forwarder tasks persist while the spawning async task awaits elsewhere. Restructure read loops to handle EOF and read errors explicitly rather than silently dropping the pipe.\n\n**Build (Mountain):**\nAdd `Proto/Vine.proto` to `tauri.conf.json` resource globs so the .proto file is available at runtime from `Contents/Resources/`.\n\nNo runtime behaviour regressions — all changes are bounded by existing gRPC retry and timeout contracts.",
			"SHA": "392f0aef133c75f34afc19f22fdd5b5a0e6bf719"
		}
	],
